        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I agree it could help with discoverability, but as this server also covers the `msgraph` provider, which is Microsoft Graph rather than Azure, an `azure_` prefix reads a little narrower than what it does.  \r\nI'm also planning on a Mason package, and Mason names packages after upstream, so it would be listed there as `ms-terraform-lsp`.  \r\nIt is hosted under `Azure` github org, so I guess it has that going in favour of the prefix as well as your discoverability argument.\r\n\r\nThanks for the feedback! Your call, I will push the rename if you still prefer the prefix.\r\n",
            "created_at": "2026-08-24T08:11:15Z",
